{"name":"Silverberry","hex":"#bebbc9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silverberry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant in the genus Elaeagnus, of about 50-70 species of deciduous or evergreen shrubs or small trees with alternate leaves, primarily native to temperate and subtropical regions of Asia.","The fruit of such a plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silverberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elaeagnus commutata","blocks":[{"text":"Elaeagnus commutata, the silverberry or wolf-willow, is a species of Elaeagnus native to western and boreal North America, from southern Alaska through British Columbia east to Quebec, south to Utah, and across the upper Midwestern United States to South Dakota and western Minnesota. It typically grows on dry to moist sandy and gravel soils in steppes, meadows or woodland edges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA.jpg/330px-Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elaeagnus_commutata"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA1.jpg/120px-Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA1.jpg/250px-Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA1.jpg/120px-Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElaeagnus_commutata_USDA1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA2.jpg/120px-Elaeagnus_commutata_USDA2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi